.TH TOTAL\-MARKDOWN 1 "2026\-11\-04" "total\-markdown 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
total\-markdown \- a fast, native, two\-pane Markdown viewer and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B total\-markdown
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Total Markdown
opens a Markdown document in two panes: the source, syntax highlighted, on
the left and the rendered preview on the right, both kept in step while you
type. It is built on Qt Widgets only — no web engine — and parses Markdown
with md4c straight into a
.B QTextDocument.
.PP
Rendered documents support CommonMark and GitHub Flavored Markdown (tables,
task lists, strikethrough, autolinks), fenced code blocks highlighted by
KDE's KSyntaxHighlighting, LaTeX formulas typeset by the bundled MicroTeX
engine, images resolved relative to the document, remote images downloaded
in the background and cached on disk, animated GIF and SVG badges, and a
size policy that keeps very large documents responsive.
.PP
If
.I file
is given, it is opened at startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Open with the source pane hidden, preview only.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/total-markdown/total-markdown.conf
User settings: theme, fonts, pane layout.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/total-markdown/remote-images
Disk cache for downloaded remote images.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/TankucT-AC/total-markdown
.UE .
